  "behavior": [
    "All layered architectures expose decoder input dimensions without native allocation; segmented inputs sum semantic token spans and prepared composites use their admitted decoder geometry.",
    "Reserved state retains the exact active request and logical frontier separately from nonrefundable backing charges. Stateless ranks advance the logical frontier without fabricating a native position.",
    "Shared transactions agree exact execution identity, batch, scheduled span length, phase, readout demand, and native state position before checkpointing or model work. One-position sequence and final-position scores are equivalent; state-only remains distinct.",
    "Decode cannot advance beyond the admitted output allowance; unknown auxiliary invocation equations cannot use an ordinary decoder quote.",
    "Successful equations must reach the checked native frontier before output observation. Transaction failure and checkpoint restoration restore logical admission alongside state without refunding backing charges.",
    "Restoring an unadmitted snapshot or presenting an unbudgeted request cannot erase an active reserved admission.",
    "Reserved prepared-input, ordinary, controlled shared-session, and sequence execution retain a native guard through publication and force completion. Guard-opening failure prevents model work; settlement failure fences further work and retains unresolved ownership.",
    "The family matrix verifies rejection before projection, exact nonzero state preservation, output-failure rollback, three valid cached decodes, restored replay through the sequence API, and renewed exhaustion rejection."
  ],
